% ============================================================================
% heat-transfer-example.query — worked recall queries against
% heat-transfer-example.adj (adj-facts-stdlib, PHYSICS).
% ============================================================================
% Three queries: forward recall with citation, backward recall (bind an
% example, find the mode), and honest abstention on a non-heat-transfer
% word (this table, like its parent heat-transfer.adj, covers the full
% three-mode domain with no abstention among the three -- but still
% abstains on anything outside that set, e.g. evaporation).
% ============================================================================

import "heat-transfer-example.adj"

% Forward: what everyday example does the cited NASA span give for conduction?
? heat_transfer_example(conduction, $Example)

% Backward: which mode does "warm air rises" illustrate?
? heat_transfer_example($Mode, warm_air_rising)

% Honest abstention: evaporation is a phase change, not one of the three heat-transfer modes.
? heat_transfer_example(evaporation, $ExampleEvap)
